WEBVTT

00:00.630 --> 00:04.980
This guy hit on me today, 
but he was <i>such</i> a dork.

00:04.980 --> 00:08.040
Well, better make up for it
 at the pool tonight.

00:08.040 --> 00:11.610
I'm waiting for you, my soulmate!

00:11.610 --> 00:12.680
Hi!

00:13.060 --> 00:16.710
May I help you find what you're looking for?

00:17.660 --> 00:19.490
You lost your wings, didn't you?

00:19.810 --> 00:23.000
Because you look like an angel.

00:26.180 --> 00:27.660
What a pickup line!

00:27.660 --> 00:29.410
I like funny guys.

00:29.410 --> 00:30.880
Nice! Then—

00:30.880 --> 00:32.630
But I don't care for playboys.

00:33.070 --> 00:35.890
Oh, come on! Just for a little while?

00:39.750 --> 00:41.020
Are you serious?

00:41.390 --> 00:44.890
You two... Are you after this card?

00:46.310 --> 00:47.400
Play!

00:51.150 --> 00:52.590
Finn, watch out!

00:52.590 --> 00:54.290
I can't see!

00:54.290 --> 00:56.660
Chris, help me! Chris!

00:55.540 --> 00:56.660
Hey, what are you...

00:56.910 --> 00:59.050
You guys seem real close.

00:59.050 --> 01:01.160
So why don't you stick together?

01:03.650 --> 01:05.100
"Love Connection"!

01:08.590 --> 01:09.690
Bye!

01:12.620 --> 01:13.820
What the heck, Finn?!

01:13.820 --> 01:14.380
Let go!

01:14.670 --> 01:15.950
What are you talking about?

01:15.950 --> 01:17.010
<i>You</i> let go!

01:17.370 --> 01:19.660
Finn, now's not the time—

01:22.160 --> 01:22.660
Huh?

01:24.000 --> 01:24.500
Huh?

01:26.970 --> 01:29.020
Are you kidding me?

03:00.270 --> 03:04.470
Scandent plants often twine around
 things due to thigmotropism.

03:04.950 --> 03:08.250
As they grow and expand,
 their tendrils move erratically,

03:08.250 --> 03:10.460
and when they find a surface...

03:10.460 --> 03:12.220
I screwed up.

03:12.220 --> 03:14.440
The power to adhere hands, huh?

03:14.440 --> 03:18.130
If Leo and Wendy find out, 
they'll make wicked fun of us.

03:18.600 --> 03:20.900
Vijay, let's keep this between us!

03:20.900 --> 03:23.010
I think they'll find out soon enough.

03:23.270 --> 03:25.890
You two sure are getting along today.

03:27.940 --> 03:29.090
On the house.

03:29.090 --> 03:31.340
I gave you two straws.

03:32.520 --> 03:35.060
L-Let's get that card already 
so I can peel you off!

03:35.060 --> 03:38.330
Yeah. I have a date this weekend.

03:38.330 --> 03:40.780
I can't wait to get you off of me.

03:43.640 --> 03:46.180
Okay! Let's go find that girl!

03:46.180 --> 03:48.910
Apparently, her name is Chelsea.

03:49.190 --> 03:49.970
What?

03:49.970 --> 03:50.540
Look.

03:51.620 --> 03:53.300
Oh, Callgram?

03:54.930 --> 03:56.540
Best of luck!

04:06.170 --> 04:08.060
Hey, what about that guy?

04:08.060 --> 04:10.430
That's a no. He's a mommy's boy.

04:11.100 --> 04:12.150
How about him?

04:12.150 --> 04:13.300
A total masochist.

04:13.300 --> 04:15.440
You're making that up.

04:15.440 --> 04:16.900
No, I'm serious!

04:16.900 --> 04:19.640
I have a good eye for men.

04:19.970 --> 04:21.940
Then what about us?

04:22.710 --> 04:24.620
Why are you here?

04:24.620 --> 04:26.200
Maybe because I'm your soulmate.

04:26.980 --> 04:28.200
In your dreams.

04:28.200 --> 04:31.720
We're in the business of collecting cards.

04:31.720 --> 04:34.960
If you undo this and 
hand yours over, we won't hurt—

04:36.690 --> 04:38.350
Stop!

04:38.350 --> 04:39.050
Finn!

04:39.050 --> 04:40.210
I-I'm sorry!

04:46.840 --> 04:47.850
Excuse us!

04:51.450 --> 04:52.910
Work with me here!

04:52.910 --> 04:54.680
That's my line!

04:54.680 --> 04:55.350
Hi!

05:01.480 --> 05:02.670
Bye!

05:04.310 --> 05:05.620
Damn it.

05:06.250 --> 05:07.740
If it weren't for this...

05:09.140 --> 05:10.620
Should we just sever it?

05:10.920 --> 05:11.690
Huh?

05:23.380 --> 05:26.130
Who knew they'd stick back together?

05:26.770 --> 05:29.630
No matter what we do, 
there's no undoing this power.

05:30.220 --> 05:31.160
Let's go, Finn!

05:31.160 --> 05:33.390
C'mon, can't we take a break?

05:34.270 --> 05:36.450
Who was that guy from yesterday?

05:36.450 --> 05:37.270
Your stalker?

05:37.630 --> 05:40.060
Maybe your soulmate?

05:40.060 --> 05:41.810
No way.

05:43.400 --> 05:44.400
Seriously?!

05:44.770 --> 05:46.270
Uh, I gotta get going!

05:46.270 --> 05:47.240
What?

05:47.240 --> 05:48.430
Chelsea?

05:54.910 --> 05:55.970
Hey, what're you doing?

05:55.970 --> 05:57.420
Wake up, Finn!

05:57.420 --> 05:59.820
Huh? Chelsea?!

06:04.200 --> 06:05.050
Bingo!

06:23.650 --> 06:24.410
Hey there.

06:25.500 --> 06:26.820
We meet again.

06:27.820 --> 06:29.180
Get in line!

06:29.180 --> 06:31.320
Hold on! I just want to talk!

06:44.190 --> 06:48.380
We've been running around town 
for three days without any sleep.

06:48.840 --> 06:50.400
I can't do this anymore.

06:50.400 --> 06:52.300
Who knew she'd be such a handful?

06:53.300 --> 06:54.730
Color me surprised.

06:55.310 --> 06:58.030
What's her deal?

06:58.030 --> 07:01.060
She doesn't even go home. 
Just hops from place to place.

07:01.770 --> 07:05.570
Hey, she doesn't seem 
like a dangerous player,

07:05.570 --> 07:07.820
so why not call it a day and get some rest?

07:10.150 --> 07:11.200
Say, Chris...

07:11.770 --> 07:13.190
Where do you live?

07:13.190 --> 07:15.490
I've never asked, but is it with family?

07:15.800 --> 07:18.250
We'll settle this today.

07:18.250 --> 07:20.210
I have an important date tomorrow.

07:22.460 --> 07:23.210
Let's go.

07:23.210 --> 07:23.710
What?

07:23.710 --> 07:25.830
Wait! I need to rest!

07:25.830 --> 07:26.440
Finn!

07:26.440 --> 07:28.530
I'm gonna go home, take a shower, and sleep!

07:29.070 --> 07:30.970
Is everything all right, you two?

07:31.570 --> 07:32.790
Mr. Apple!

07:33.780 --> 07:35.730
Fighting out in public?

07:36.380 --> 07:37.470
Hmm?

07:39.220 --> 07:42.930
Wait, hang on! I think you've got 
totally the wrong idea right now!

07:43.980 --> 07:47.530
Hope to see you again at the dealership!

07:56.360 --> 07:57.990
Cut this out already!

07:57.990 --> 08:00.530
Took the words right out of my mouth.

08:00.530 --> 08:03.740
You've been wandering around, 
not even going home...

08:03.740 --> 08:05.830
I don't have a home.

08:06.950 --> 08:11.370
I couch surf at my friends' places,
 and I move around for work and fun.

08:11.720 --> 08:15.140
You meet more people that way, y'know?

08:15.140 --> 08:16.950
Why are you doing all that?

08:16.950 --> 08:19.330
To find my soulmate.

08:19.330 --> 08:20.170
Huh?

08:20.170 --> 08:23.690
When I find them, 
I don't want to let go of them.

08:23.690 --> 08:25.650
If I use the power of my card...

08:27.310 --> 08:28.490
It'll be perfect.

08:29.170 --> 08:31.690
That's a weird way of looking at it.

08:31.690 --> 08:34.990
Listen, you're very attractive.

08:34.990 --> 08:37.690
So stop relying on the power of that card.

08:37.690 --> 08:39.390
Now you're lecturing me?

08:39.830 --> 08:41.500
No thanks. I'm not interested.

08:41.920 --> 08:43.290
I totally get that.

08:43.290 --> 08:45.270
I'm annoying, aren't I?

08:45.270 --> 08:46.840
So how about this?

08:46.840 --> 08:50.630
In exchange for your card, 
I'll do whatever you say.

08:51.060 --> 08:53.890
If you want money, 
I'll write you a blank check.

08:53.890 --> 08:55.510
Just fill in the number.

08:56.050 --> 08:59.530
If you want something sweet, 
I'll get you treats from all over Fourland.

08:59.530 --> 09:02.980
If you want, I'll even make you a princess.

09:03.460 --> 09:04.890
Your words don't resonate with me.

09:05.830 --> 09:07.400
They don't move my heart at all.

09:07.830 --> 09:09.070
Then how about—

09:09.070 --> 09:11.280
Y'know, you're as empty as I thought.

09:11.720 --> 09:13.030
Empty?

09:13.030 --> 09:15.700
Empty words, empty attitude.

09:15.700 --> 09:18.030
There's nothing real about you.

09:18.030 --> 09:20.220
You know me so well.

09:20.650 --> 09:23.700
I've got a good eye for men.

09:24.540 --> 09:27.090
Do you do this to everyone?

09:27.090 --> 09:30.790
Flashing that smile, 
putting on that mask of lies...

09:31.310 --> 09:33.950
Call me empty, call me a liar. 
This is who I am.

09:34.260 --> 09:35.050
Got a problem?

09:36.460 --> 09:38.050
That's pretty sad.

09:38.290 --> 09:39.430
Hey, wait!

09:39.910 --> 09:41.080
Come on, Finn!

09:41.080 --> 09:43.070
It's not happening, Chris.

09:43.070 --> 09:45.780
Let's take a break at my place and regroup.

09:45.780 --> 09:48.100
I don't have time! Tomorrow...

09:48.400 --> 09:50.400
What's the hurry?

09:50.400 --> 09:51.480
You're acting strange.

10:16.490 --> 10:18.920
No updates.

10:19.800 --> 10:20.730
I'm gonna sleep a bit.

10:20.730 --> 10:21.260
Huh?

10:22.170 --> 10:23.830
Hey, that's my bed...

10:26.170 --> 10:27.160
Jeez.

11:01.340 --> 11:02.970
Did you have a bad dream?

11:03.740 --> 11:05.240
I didn't know you were awake.

11:05.690 --> 11:08.310
It's hard to sleep with a different pillow.

11:10.310 --> 11:13.660
I have this nightmare every now and then

11:14.340 --> 11:16.850
where a black suit of armor attacks me.

11:17.850 --> 11:21.070
The doctor said it could be trauma
 from the accident or whatever.

11:21.810 --> 11:22.690
The accident?

11:22.690 --> 11:24.950
Yeah, when I was seven.

11:26.090 --> 11:28.330
I lost my parents and big brother.

11:28.330 --> 11:30.260
I don't remember much, though.

11:30.260 --> 11:32.050
I was raised in an orphanage after that.

11:37.170 --> 11:38.960
Still no updates?

11:39.630 --> 11:42.970
Maybe she realized we were checking it.

11:45.450 --> 11:47.470
I guess time's up.

11:48.200 --> 11:50.690
Finn, can you promise me something?

11:52.250 --> 11:54.440
Don't tell a soul about what you see today.

11:55.190 --> 11:57.460
Not even the members of High Card.

11:58.090 --> 11:58.850
Huh?

11:59.720 --> 12:00.470
Please.

12:07.340 --> 12:08.180
Sorry.

12:09.010 --> 12:11.010
Did I keep you waiting, Michel?

12:11.010 --> 12:13.330
Nope, I just got here.

12:13.330 --> 12:15.000
That's good.

12:15.410 --> 12:17.800
So this <i>is</i> just a regular date...

12:17.800 --> 12:19.530
Big Brother, who is this?

12:20.220 --> 12:21.540
"Big Brother"?!

12:21.540 --> 12:23.910
This is Finn, a coworker of mine.

12:23.910 --> 12:27.390
You've never introduced 
a colleague to me before!

12:28.060 --> 12:30.630
He's a new employee, but he's really good.

12:30.630 --> 12:32.570
And a very nice guy.

12:32.570 --> 12:34.500
Chris, I didn't know you had sis—

12:34.500 --> 12:36.290
Just go along with it.

12:36.290 --> 12:37.170
Shall we?

12:37.170 --> 12:37.970
Sure!

12:39.570 --> 12:42.360
I've really been looking forward to this.

12:42.360 --> 12:44.330
There are so many places I want to go!

12:45.400 --> 12:47.460
Where to first, then?

12:48.270 --> 12:49.160
Um...

12:49.160 --> 12:49.910
Hmm?

12:50.250 --> 12:52.900
Please be good to my brother.

12:52.900 --> 12:53.540
Huh?

12:53.540 --> 12:55.170
I mean, you two are...

12:57.420 --> 12:58.670
I think it's great!

12:58.910 --> 13:01.090
N-No! It's the card—

13:01.090 --> 13:02.900
Ouch!

13:05.660 --> 13:07.840
Of course, Michel.

13:08.770 --> 13:09.850
Great!

13:13.070 --> 13:14.350
You know, Finn,

13:14.350 --> 13:18.360
my brother's always been kind to me 
 ever since we were little.

13:19.190 --> 13:24.360
So much so that sometimes 
I think he's spoiling me.

13:24.780 --> 13:28.620
He can be overprotective and a worrywart.

13:30.010 --> 13:32.960
What's he like at work?

13:32.960 --> 13:35.530
Huh? Uh...

13:36.050 --> 13:39.890
He's nice to everyone at work too. 
We all trust him lots.

13:40.250 --> 13:41.580
I'm so glad!

13:42.730 --> 13:43.720
Are you okay?!

13:44.220 --> 13:45.590
Just some ice cream in my throat.

13:45.590 --> 13:47.010
Are you sure you're okay?

13:47.310 --> 13:49.650
I told you I'm fine!

13:49.650 --> 13:51.390
You see what I mean?

13:51.650 --> 13:53.630
He's always like this.

13:58.490 --> 14:00.370
Pardon me. I'm going to the ladies' room.

14:03.220 --> 14:06.570
You're a good brother in front of her.

14:07.480 --> 14:09.530
Thanks for playing along.

14:10.190 --> 14:13.230
I haven't told her anything about High Card.

14:15.260 --> 14:16.380
Really?

14:16.940 --> 14:19.540
You're lying to your sister?

14:19.540 --> 14:20.920
Chelsea?!

14:21.210 --> 14:22.080
What gives?

14:22.080 --> 14:23.000
Working part-time.

14:23.000 --> 14:24.870
What are <i>you</i> doing here?

14:24.870 --> 14:27.240
I stopped posting on Callgram.

14:27.240 --> 14:29.550
My sister wanted to come here.

14:30.150 --> 14:35.260
Must be hard switching from
 a flirt to a kind brother.

14:35.260 --> 14:37.930
I guess you can play any part 
since you're empty.

14:38.210 --> 14:40.440
Yup. Artful, aren't I?

14:41.940 --> 14:43.940
You're a sad man.

14:44.350 --> 14:46.350
Are you friends with my brother?

14:46.350 --> 14:47.900
What?! Friends?

14:47.900 --> 14:48.520
This guy's—

14:48.520 --> 14:50.190
Yeah, she's a friend.

14:50.190 --> 14:52.450
She just happens to work here.

14:52.450 --> 14:55.770
Yeah, that's right! We're all super close!

14:55.770 --> 14:56.860
That's great!

14:57.500 --> 15:00.820
Oh, I know! We're headed over 
 to the River Side Garden.

15:00.820 --> 15:02.130
Would you care to join us?

15:02.130 --> 15:02.580
Huh?

15:02.800 --> 15:05.080
Michel, she's working right now.

15:05.080 --> 15:05.960
I'll go.

15:06.780 --> 15:07.840
What?

15:08.090 --> 15:09.790
I'm coming with you.

15:12.590 --> 15:15.340
This is so nice!

15:15.650 --> 15:17.380
What's the big idea?

15:17.380 --> 15:18.610
Revenge.

15:18.610 --> 15:21.860
I'll rip off your mask 
in front of your sister.

15:22.330 --> 15:23.730
Wait up!

15:23.950 --> 15:26.110
Hey, is this going to work?

15:29.030 --> 15:30.490
Hey, Chris.

15:30.490 --> 15:34.970
You never miss a chance to flirt with me,
 but you're awfully quiet today.

15:34.970 --> 15:37.120
That's a funny joke.

15:37.120 --> 15:40.120
Chelsea's the one who got
 me and Finn together.

15:40.120 --> 15:41.570
That's great!

15:43.500 --> 15:45.500
Hey, Chris.

15:45.500 --> 15:48.090
You really scared me the other day.

15:48.090 --> 15:49.980
I was in my bathing suit, and you—

15:49.980 --> 15:53.260
Chelsea's currently looking for her soulmate.

15:53.260 --> 15:54.390
We should leave her to it.

15:56.410 --> 15:57.700
Chelsea!

15:58.140 --> 16:01.590
They have pendants to help 
you find your soulmate!

16:01.590 --> 16:02.890
Really?!

16:11.860 --> 16:13.170
That's cold!

16:13.720 --> 16:15.160
Come on, Chris!

16:15.160 --> 16:17.730
<i>Crap, I'm letting her lead me by the nose!</i>

16:17.730 --> 16:20.280
<i>I'm supposed to be exposing that guy...</i>

16:23.810 --> 16:25.260
We can do that later.

16:25.800 --> 16:27.840
Michel, let's take pictures!

16:28.110 --> 16:28.840
Okay!

16:30.340 --> 16:32.010
Hey, lookin' good!

16:32.010 --> 16:32.910
It is a good one!

16:32.910 --> 16:34.840
Seems like they're having fun.

16:48.010 --> 16:49.300
You must be tired.

16:49.300 --> 16:50.980
Let's get you home.

16:51.240 --> 16:54.530
Before we go, I want to ride 
the Ferris wheel in Pott Park.

16:55.000 --> 16:58.340
Remember that time the three of us
 did it when we were little?

16:58.930 --> 17:02.500
The city looked so pretty from the top...

17:03.060 --> 17:04.410
I remember.

17:04.920 --> 17:06.840
But we'll save that for next time.

17:07.270 --> 17:08.450
You have my word.

17:08.450 --> 17:09.480
But...

17:09.480 --> 17:11.860
What's the big deal? 
Let's hit the Ferris wheel.

17:11.860 --> 17:13.490
Kindly stay out of this.

17:13.830 --> 17:15.880
We can stay a bit longer, can't we?

17:16.200 --> 17:17.890
Stay out of this.

17:18.180 --> 17:19.750
Cut it out, you two.

17:19.750 --> 17:22.930
You're seriously acting
 like bickering lovers.

17:24.200 --> 17:25.180
Michel!

17:27.090 --> 17:28.100
What's wrong?!

17:28.680 --> 17:31.830
Chris...

17:33.000 --> 17:33.830
Michel!

17:33.830 --> 17:35.090
L-Let's call an ambulance!

17:35.090 --> 17:36.070
There's no time!

17:36.560 --> 17:38.060
Undo this! Now!

17:39.170 --> 17:40.310
Come on!

17:49.790 --> 17:53.210
<i>It's the result of a genetic disorder.</i>

17:53.210 --> 17:56.130
<i>She's afflicted just like her late mother,</i>

17:56.130 --> 17:59.190
<i>and there's no effective 
cure for it at the moment.</i>

17:59.190 --> 18:00.300
<i>Michel.</i>

18:01.070 --> 18:03.890
<i>I'm going to save you. I promise.</i>

18:11.560 --> 18:12.590
Michel!

18:12.590 --> 18:14.440
You need to wait out here.

18:14.440 --> 18:16.950
But she needs me!

18:18.860 --> 18:20.200
Stop it, Chris!

18:20.430 --> 18:21.960
Shut up! Out of my way!

18:28.060 --> 18:29.690
Calm down, Chris.

18:42.780 --> 18:45.990
Mr. Redgrave, the doctor 
would like to speak with you.

18:48.980 --> 18:51.230
I'm okay now.

18:54.450 --> 18:59.740
To be frank, your sister is in no 
condition to be out and about.

19:00.280 --> 19:03.620
It seems she snuck out of the hospital.

19:04.130 --> 19:06.840
But she told me she's been doing better.

19:08.120 --> 19:10.870
That's a lie, I'm afraid.

19:11.460 --> 19:14.300
She doesn't want to worry you

19:14.300 --> 19:17.010
because she understands 
what's happening to her.

19:17.010 --> 19:19.000
What do you mean?

19:19.310 --> 19:20.500
Doctor...

19:20.500 --> 19:22.760
Please listen carefully.

19:23.560 --> 19:24.950
You sister is...

19:26.260 --> 19:29.620
I see. So you've been in the 
hospital for a long while, huh?

19:29.620 --> 19:34.150
Yes. And Chris used to come 
visit me all the time.

19:34.520 --> 19:38.280
He's all the family I've got,
 but he goes overboard.

19:38.280 --> 19:39.150
What?

19:39.490 --> 19:41.900
What about your parents, Michel?

19:44.220 --> 19:46.430
So Chris is an orphan too...

19:51.330 --> 19:52.550
Chris.

20:03.070 --> 20:04.930
Is Michel going to be okay?

20:04.930 --> 20:07.450
She just had a little too much fun today.

20:07.890 --> 20:09.310
She'll be fine.

20:09.590 --> 20:10.310
You liar.

20:11.950 --> 20:14.940
This is the hospice ward, right?

20:14.940 --> 20:16.700
Then, Michel is...

20:17.160 --> 20:19.770
You're gonna lie about your sister too?

20:19.770 --> 20:24.570
Kind lies help you forget 
hard truths and sad times.

20:24.970 --> 20:27.470
They don't hurt anyone.

20:27.990 --> 20:28.850
Right?

20:29.290 --> 20:32.100
Isn't it hurting you, though?

20:33.020 --> 20:34.110
I'm fine.

20:34.570 --> 20:37.090
I'm an immortal ladies' man.

20:38.020 --> 20:43.610
Even if there comes a time I'm not,
 I'll just put on another mask.

20:44.030 --> 20:45.700
A mask of lies.

20:46.840 --> 20:48.910
I'm empty, like you pointed out.

20:48.910 --> 20:52.150
Even if I take off my mask, 
there's nothing to see behind it.

20:53.500 --> 20:55.960
I think I've seen it.

20:57.340 --> 20:59.440
The face under your mask.

21:04.790 --> 21:07.950
You can have my card when I change my mind.

21:09.310 --> 21:11.540
I don't know when that's going to be.

21:12.090 --> 21:15.480
But maybe someday I won't need it anymore.

21:15.990 --> 21:17.550
Okay.

21:17.550 --> 21:20.230
As a thank-you for keeping us company today,

21:21.010 --> 21:23.970
I'll come pick it up from you
 when that time comes.

22:58.100 --> 23:00.380
The usual, please.

23:01.490 --> 23:04.620
Mr. Apple hasn't been back 
to the store since that day.

23:04.620 --> 23:06.730
Maybe he did totally get the wrong idea.

23:06.730 --> 23:08.360
Don't even joke.

23:08.360 --> 23:09.560
Here you are.

23:09.560 --> 23:10.930
Thank you.

23:11.490 --> 23:13.200
Wh-What're you doing here?!

23:13.200 --> 23:15.370
I decided to get a job here.

23:15.370 --> 23:17.070
She's our new live-in server.

23:17.070 --> 23:21.750
I thought you were going from place to place
 in search of your soulmate.

23:21.750 --> 23:24.850
If you live and work here, 
doesn't that limit the people you meet?

23:24.850 --> 23:26.790
I thought I'd give it a chance.

23:27.710 --> 23:30.860
To see if I don't need the card anymore.

23:32.140 --> 23:33.010
Huh?

23:33.860 --> 23:35.010
What does that mean?

23:36.810 --> 23:39.510
Next time: "HEAT UP."
